[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111244184","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111244184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111244184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DJuY","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:53:43Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T14:53:43Z","body":"Hello humans, I'm @editorialbot, a robot that can help you with some common editorial tasks.\n\nFor a list of things I can do to help you, just type:\n\n```\n@editorialbot commands\n```\n\nFor example, to regenerate the paper pdf after making changes in the paper's md or bib files, type:\n\n```\n@editorialbot generate pdf\n```\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111244184/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111254362","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111254362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111254362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DMNa","user":{"login":"majensen","id":82073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyMDcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen","html_url":"https://github.com/majensen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:07Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T23:13:26Z","body":"> # JOSS Review — PAI: The Pulmonary Agent-based Infection Simulator\n> **Reviewer:** @dcnickle\n> **Issue:** openjournals/joss-reviews#8411\n> **Software version reviewed:** v1.0.0\n> **Docker image:** `ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai:latest` (digest `sha256:a77fa8b8d74b9354e9ddd552608cc545c4936ff0fbeafd1bb7e462a0031bb72d`)\n> **Review platform:** macOS (Apple Silicon, aarch64) with Docker Desktop 29.2.1, `--platform linux/amd64`\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Conflict of Interest\n> \n> - [x] I confirm that I have read the JOSS [conflict of interest policy]\n> \n> ## Code of Conduct\n> \n> - [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct]\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## General Checks\n> \n> - [x] **Repository:** Source code is publicly available at https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI.\n> - [x] **License:** MIT License, confirmed valid OSI-approved open source license.\n> - [x] **Contribution and authorship:** The submitting author (@deassisinfo, 63 commits) has made major contributions. A second author (henriquedeassis, 39 commits) has also contributed substantially. Authorship is consistent with commit history.\n> - [x] **Substantial scholarly effort:** The software has been applied in at least three peer-reviewed publications (Ribeiro 2022, Ribeiro 2023, Qu 2025) and implements a multi-scale, multi-language agent-based modeling framework with non-trivial biological scope.\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Functionality\n> \n> - [x] **Installation:** The Docker image pulls and runs successfully via `docker pull --platform linux/amd64 ghcr.io/nutritionallungimmunity/pai:latest`. The image is functional.\n> \n>   > **Required fix:** The image is built only for `linux/amd64`. On Apple Silicon (aarch64), users must explicitly pass `--platform linux/amd64` or the pull will fail with `no matching manifest for linux/arm64/v8`. This must be documented in the README. A multi-arch build (adding `linux/arm64`) would be better.\n> \n> - [x] **Functionality:** Both the C++ (`PAI++`) and Java (`jPAI`) implementations execute simulations and produce time-series output. The built-in test suites (`ctest`, `jtest`) pass on the first attempt. Key state variables — *Aspergillus fumigatus* burden, TNF-α, and macrophage counts — are verified within expected ranges at six time points (t = 0, 180, 360, 720, 1440, and 2145 minutes) across two simulation runs per implementation.\n> \n> - [x] **Performance:** `Benchmark.pdf` was provided and reviewed. It contains 8 figures (S1–S8) covering output fidelity, runtime, and memory across 100 simulation runs each.\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Documentation\n> \n> - [x] **Installation instructions:** There are no instructions for users who wish to build from source (C++ compilation flags, JDK version requirements, linking the precompiled C++ modules into the Java layer). Non-Docker users have no clear way to installation.\n> \n> - [x] **Example usage:** There is no worked example in the documentation. The `cpp` entrypoint prints usage (`./PAIpp <t0> <Aspergillus> <Macrophage> <Pneumocyte>`) when called without arguments, but no example showing biologically meaningful initial conditions, expected runtime, or how to redirect and interpret the output is provided.\n> \n> - [x] **Functionality documentation:** Both implementations write simulation output exclusively to stdout as space-delimited numerical columns with no header row. The C++ implementation produces 20 columns; the Java implementation produces 24. The paper explains that jPAI \"contains other pieces of code not discussed here,\" which accounts for the divergence, but this is not documented anywhere for the user. The paper also states that documentation is provided only for the Java version; this limitation should be stated explicitly in the README.\n> \n> - [x] **Automated tests:** Both implementations include regression test suites (`ctest` for PAI++, `jtest` for jPAI) that run simulations and assert that state variables remain within biologically expected ranges. Tests pass.\n> \n> - [x] **Community guidelines:** No `CONTRIBUTING.md` or equivalent document is present. There are no stated guidelines for reporting bugs, requesting features, or contributing code.\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Software Paper\n> \n> - [x] **Summary:** Present. PAI is described as a multi-scale ABM of the pulmonary immune response to *Aspergillus fumigatus*, implemented in both Java and C++, operating on a 3D voxelized alveolar space with intracellular models, molecular diffusion, and immune cell recruitment.\n> \n> - [x] **Statement of need:** I think this is good. The authors provide epidemiological context (30–60% mortality in invasive aspergillosis, 10–14% incidence in ICU COVID-19 patients) and clearly articulate the limitation of ODE/PDE models in representing discrete cellular interactions and spatial heterogeneity.\n> \n> - [x] **State of the field:** The paper distinguishes PAI from ODE/PDE-based approaches and positions it relative to existing ABM frameworks, citing prior applications of the model.\n> \n> - [x] **Software availability statement:** The paper has no explicit software availability section. The repository URL and version appear in the JOSS submission metadata but are not stated in the paper body.\n> \n> - [x] **Quality of writing:** The writing is generally clear.\n>   - The paper does not describe the output format, column names, or units, making it impossible for a new user to connect the stdout stream to the described biology without consulting prior publications.\n> \n> \n> - [x] **References:** Nine references have missing or unverified DOIs as flagged by editorialbot. \n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Bug Reports\n> \n> The following bugs were identified during functional testing and must be addressed:\n> \n> **Bug 1 — Java crashes without arguments (Minor)**\n> Running `docker run ... java` with no arguments raises an unhandled `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException: Index 0 out of bounds for length 0` at `Main.java:38`. The C++ entrypoint handles the missing-arguments case gracefully by printing usage. The Java entrypoint must do the same.\n> \n> ---\n> \n> ## Summary Assessment\n> \n> The software is functional, tests pass, and the biological motivation is sound. The codebase represents a scholarly effort applied to a clinically important problem.  \n\n _Originally posted by @DavidNickle in [#8411](https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/8411#issuecomment-4111183277)_","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111254362/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111256860","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111256860","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111256860,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DM0c","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:28Z","body":"## Repository Analysis Report\n\n### Code breakdown\n\n```\ngithub.com/AlDanial/cloc v 1.98  T=0.15 s (1801.0 files/s, 172611.6 lines/s)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLanguage                     files          blank        comment           code\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJava                           106           2190           3352           7946\nC++                             41            814            455           3708\nC/C++ Header                    56            941            564           2715\nD                               41              0              0           1614\nMarkdown                         5            215              0            611\nmake                            13            125             68            370\nPython                           2             62              0            247\nXML                              5              0              0            238\nINI                              4              0              0            140\nTeX                              1             13              0            139\nDockerfile                       1             15              8             24\nBourne Shell                     1              2              0             20\nCMake                            1             12             10             20\nJupyter Notebook                 1              0              6              0\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSUM:                           278           4389           4463          17792\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n```\n\n#### Commit Count by Author\n\n```\n63\tdeassisinfo\n    51\thenriquedeassis\n     2\tTsiorintsoa\n     1\tstsiori\n```\n\n## Repository History\n\n**Repository age:** First commit on October 21, 2022\n\n\n**Code distribution (top 3 48-hour windows):**\n\n| Period | Insertions | % of Total | Signal | View Changes |\n|--------|------------|------------|--------|-------------|\n| Jun 11, 2025 - Jun 13, 2025 | 47950 | 70.4% | 🟠 | [View diff](https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/compare/93e8f79cdfd65491d56a83438109ed450a72e992^...101fa036dddb764d4c496fb46c6cda2512a331ed) |\n| Jun 04, 2025 - Jun 06, 2025 | 5428 | 8.0% | 🟢 | [View diff](https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/compare/d292fedf72b9b81b935efcbfd9e5b266e9c0e2c7^...22c4356d2a437c8edf5491c388934661726cc624) |\n| Feb 20, 2024 - Feb 22, 2024 | 3776 | 5.5% | 🟢 | [View commit](https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI/commit/ed02157233a57d8c69c69a5607b89efd51dd609b) |\n\n\n## GitHub Activity Metrics\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|--------|------:|\n| GitHub stars | 0 |\n| Forks | 1 |\n| GitHub contributors | 2 |\n| Releases | 0 |\n| Total issues | 1 |\n| Total pull requests | 0 |\n| Unique commenters/reviewers (excluding authors) | 0 |\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111256860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111256986","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111256986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111256986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DM2a","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:29Z","body":"**Paper file info**:\n\n📄 Wordcount for `paper.md` is **1106**\n\n✅ The paper includes a `Statement of need` section\n\n🔴 Failed to discover a `State of the field` section in paper\n\n🔴 Failed to discover a `Software design` section in paper\n\n🔴 Failed to discover a `Research impact statement` section in paper\n\n🔴 Failed to discover an `AI usage disclosure` section in paper\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111256986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111257461","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111257461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111257461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DM91","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:32Z","body":"**License info**:\n\n✅ License found: `MIT License` (Valid open source [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses) license)\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111257461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111257614","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4111257614","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4111257614,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs71DNAO","user":{"login":"majensen","id":82073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyMDcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen","html_url":"https://github.com/majensen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majensen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:55:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T19:58:44Z","body":"## Review checklist for @majensen\n\n### AI usage\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS AI policy](https://joss.theoj.org/about#ai-policy) and understand that:\n  - AI may only be used for **non-substantive assistance** (e.g., grammar checking my review text, contextualizing public materials)\n  - **All evaluative decisions**—including scoring, accept/reject recommendations, and assessments of originality, correctness, significance, and ethics compliance—**must be made exclusively by me**, not AI\n  - I bear full responsibility for all judgments, recommendations, and technical claims in my review\n  - I will disclose any AI assistance at the conclusion of my review\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI](https://github.com/NutritionalLungImmunity/PAI)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@deassisinfo) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Scope and significance:** Does this submission demonstrate clear research impact or credible scholarly significance as described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/submitting.html)?\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n### Development history and open-source practice\n\n- [x] **Development timeline:** Does the project show evidence of sustained development over time (preferably months or years) rather than rapid, recent code generation?\n- [x] **Open development:** Was the software developed openly from early stages? For projects with recent public repositories, is there at least six months of public development history with evidence of releases, public issues/pull requests, and ideally external engagement?\n- [x] **Collaborative effort:** Does the project show evidence of community engagement such as contributions from multiple developers, issues/discussions from external users, or community influence on the development described in the paper?\n- [x] **Good practices:** Does the project look like a reusable, non-throwaway research software project that follows good open-source practices (license, documentation, tests and/or verification processes, releases, and clear contribution/support pathways).\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary (required section):** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need (required section):** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field (required section):** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages? If related tools exist, do they provide a clear \"build vs. contribute\" justification explaining their unique scholarly contribution and why alternatives are insufficient?\n- [x] **Software Design (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Software Design\" section that explains the trade-offs weighed, the design/architecture chosen, and why it matters? Is the content compelling and does it demonstrate meaningful design thinking?\n- [x] **Research Impact Statement (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Research Impact Statement\" section providing evidence of realized impact (publications, external use, integrations) or credible near-term significance (benchmarks, reproducible materials, community-readiness signals)? Is the evidence presented compelling?\n- [x] **AI usage disclosure (required section):** Does the paper include an \"AI usage disclosure\" section that transparently discloses any use of generative AI in the software creation, documentation, or paper authoring?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4111257614/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4137677381","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245#issuecomment-4137677381","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10245","id":4137677381,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs72n_JF","user":{"login":"deassisinfo","id":32418684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNDE4Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32418684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo","html_url":"https://github.com/deassisinfo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deassisinfo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T19:31:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T19:31:45Z","body":"We have fixed the bug with the Java version (Java with no parameters), and we have expanded both Java and C++ to show a usage example with a meaningful biological initial value from my Paper (Ribeiro, HAL et al. 2022). We will also indicate that on the README.md shortly. We also added the column names in both Java and C++.\n\nWe would also like to point out that both Java and C++ output the same 24 columns. The reviewers must be working with a slightly outdated version of the code. As for the pieces of code in Java that are not discussed, that is true, but those parts are not being executed and should not create any divergence. We only find minimal divergence between Java and C++, which we attributed to implementation differences. But again, those are minimal. \n\nWe are working on the other issues the reviewers pointed out, including the Apple Silicon (aarch64) image problem and the revisions needed in the paper, README.md, and other materials.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4137677381/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4187809525","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/j